---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Ramen from '../../components/Ramen.astro'
import ProjectPage from '../../components/ProjectPage.astro'
---

<Layout>
  <ProjectPage title="Primitives ramen bowl">
    <Ramen slot="project-code" />

    <Fragment slot="project-description">
      <p>
        For this (pork shôyu) ramen bowl (with an extra egg), I wanted to make a
        scene using only Three.js primitives. So we have : BoxGeometries,
        CylinderGeometries, SphereGeometries, RingGeometries, CircleGeometries,
        PlaneGeometries and TorusGeometries and TorusKnotGeometries (for the
        noodles). Lots of groups are used to gather the meshes by "theme" (a.k.a
        ingredients in most cases), and some loops are used to duplicate and
        place them in the scene.
      </p>
      <p>
        I used the MeshStandardMaterial this time so I had to parameter a few
        lights too : an AmbientLight, an HemisphereLight and 2 PointLights. I
        wanted to keep things simple for the materials, so I didn't use any map,
        but played with color, roughness, metalness and emissive properties
        instead.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </ProjectPage>
</Layout>
